     2| * IVX Registration Orchestrator — Phase 2 reliability hardening.
     3| *
     4| * Wraps the existing `registerMember` pipeline with:
     5| *  - idempotency via `registrationRequestId` (one key = one logical registration)
     6| *  - explicit state machine (IDLE → VALIDATING → … → COMPLETED / RECOVERABLE_ERROR / BLOCKED)
     7| *  - partial-failure recovery (Auth exists / member missing / interest missing / session missing)
     8| *  - normalized error format with stable codes + traceId (no raw stack traces, no secrets)
     9| *  - bounded retries with exponential backoff (network / 5xx only — never for validation / auth / duplicates)
    10| *  - durable persistence of registration state so a timeout or browser refresh can resume safely
    11| *  - production-safe telemetry (no passwords, tokens, PII in logs)
    12| *
    13| * Security invariants:
    14| *  - passwords are NEVER logged, persisted to durable store, or included in telemetry
    15| *  - access / refresh tokens are NEVER persisted to durable store
    16| *  - only the normalized email hash + request ID + stage + timestamps are persisted
    17| *
    18| * Endpoint surface:
    19| *  - POST /api/members/register            (existing, now accepts registrationRequestId)
    20| *  - GET  /api/ivx/registration/status?id=  (resume / inspect existing request)
    21| *  - GET  /api/ivx/registration/health      (config + Supabase + tables reachable)
    22| */
